= Memory — Simple =

'''Memory''' is how past experience can affect what you know, think, or do later.

Memory is not like a perfect video recording.

Information has to be encoded. Later it may be kept, changed, strengthened, mixed with other information, or forgotten. When you remember something, your mind reconstructs it using memory traces and current cues.

There are several kinds of memory, including memory for events, facts, skills, and information you are using right now.

[[Working memory/Simple|Working memory]] is the limited system used to keep information active during a task.

A strong feeling of confidence does not always mean a memory is accurate.

